        "body": "A short cross-reference to the system entry saves the next owner a search. The entry should show the requested change and the approved change side by side. When a field is unknown, write unknown rather than leaving it blank. The escalation rule file should keep the original submission and the checked version together. In the what the escalation trigger entry must show step, the written action is to test each trigger against one real case before launch.\n\nA entry with a named origin and a timestamp can survive a staffing change. The owner should be able to tell whether the proof came from a person, a system, or a document. Store the escalation trigger entry where the next owner can find it without asking.\n\nThe escalation rule entry is strongest when a new owner can read it without a second message thread. Four facts carry escalation trigger: what arrived, what was verified, who approved it, and where the result now lives. The entry should show the difference between what was requested and what was actually changed."
