        "body": "A resolution note should be short enough to read and specific enough to confirm. The analyst resolutions the preparation; the owner resolutions the decision. The best resolution is the one the next owner can confirm in under a minute. A measured resolution rate without a definition is just a number with confidence. In the how to confirm and resolve step, the written action is to flag any message that differs from the approved summary.\n\nThe client communication review should look at the oldest resolution, not only the newest. A request that needed a correction is useful proof about the routine. The client update entry should distinguish a confirmed resolution from an assumed one.\n\nFor offshore program owners and operations leaders, a defensible resolution is worth more than a fast one. Keep the resolution rule fixed for the review window so the comparison means something. Close the client update only after the destination entry shows the approved change."
